# Corner Smoothing (平滑圆角)

Every rounded corner in this project uses **Figma/iOS squircle** at **60%** smoothing. Do not rely on plain CSS `border-radius` alone for final appearance.

## Token & runtime

- Smoothing level: `--corner-smoothing: 0.6` (in `packages/tokens/spec/scale/semantic.json`)
- Radius tokens: `var(--radius-xs|sm|md|lg|full)` — never hardcode px radii in components
- Global init (already wired): `initCornerSmoothing()` in Storybook `preview.ts`
- Engine: `@eds/desktop-tokens/corner-smoothing` (bundles `figma-squircle`, applies `clip-path: path(...)`)

## CSS rules

- Put `border-radius` on **the element that is visually rounded** (the painted surface), not only on a wrapper with `overflow: hidden`.
- Prefer radius tokens over `--scale-*` unless matching an existing effect spec (e.g. `effect-flotation-box` uses `var(--radius-md)`).

```css
/* ❌ BAD — radius on wrapper; img won't get squircle */
.logo { border-radius: var(--radius-md); overflow: hidden; }
.logoImage { display: block; }

/* ✅ GOOD — radius on the visible element */
.logoImage { border-radius: var(--radius-md); }
```

- Do **not** add per-component squircle JS or custom `clip-path` — the global scanner binds all non-zero `border-radius` automatically.
- Opt out only when squircle breaks an effect: `data-no-corner-smoothing` on element or ancestor.

## Effect boxes

- Apply smoothing on elements with `border-radius` except `.effect-container-box` / `.effect-flotation-box` / `.effect-popup-box` (clip-path would clip their `box-shadow`).
- Do not duplicate `clip-path` on effect sub-layers.

## Dynamic UI (Teleport / v-if)

After async mount, rescan so elements with layout get bound:

```ts
import { rescanCornerSmoothing } from '@eds/desktop-tokens/corner-smoothing';

nextTick(() => {
  if (rootRef.value) rescanCornerSmoothing(rootRef.value);
});
```

## Known limits

- `clip-path` may clip outer `box-shadow` on the same element; use opt-out if glow is critical.
- `%` radii (e.g. `50%` circles) are skipped — already continuous curves.
